---
const steps = [
  {
    ord: "Step 01 / 03",
    title: "Download the matching build",
    body: "Keep the activation key from Gumroad and download the package matched to your Sublime Text build.",
    code: "Choose the download for your Sublime build",
  },
  {
    ord: "Step 02 / 03",
    title: "Install and activate",
    body: "Copy Limitcode.sublime-package into Installed Packages, restart Sublime, then activate the device from the Command Palette.",
    code: "Command Palette → Limitcode Pro: Activate License",
  },
  {
    ord: "Step 03 / 03",
    title: "Connect a provider",
    body: "Add an API key, sign in with a supported account, use an existing CLI login, or point Limitcode at a local endpoint. Then open Limitcode Chat.",
    code: "Command Palette → Limitcode: Setup Provider API Key",
  },
];
---

<section id="install" class="container">
  <div class="section-head">
    <span class="section-num">07 - Installation</span>
    <h2>From download to first task in three steps.</h2>
    <p>No separate daemon is required. API-key providers work directly from the plugin; account, CLI, and local integrations use their own optional setup.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="install-steps">
    {steps.map((s) => (
      <article class="install">
        <span class="ord">{s.ord}</span>
        <h3>{s.title}</h3>
        <p>{s.body}</p>
        <div class="code"><span class="c">$</span> {s.code.replace(/^\$\s*/, "")}</div>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>

  <a class="docs-link" href="mailto:hola@jawuil.dev?subject=Limitcode%20Pro%20installation">
    Need installation help? Email Jawuil →
  </a>
</section>
